<title>NEW ZEALAND: New New Zealand cabinet list.</title>
<headline>New New Zealand cabinet list.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are members of the National-New Zealand First coalition cabinet, announced on Sunday by Prime Minister Jim Bolger. Ministers are from the National Party unless otherwise stated.</p>
<p>THE CABINET:</p>
<p>    Jim Bolger		  Prime Minister</p>
<p>    Winston Peters (NZF)    Deputy Prime Minister</p>
<p>				    Treasurer</p>
<p>    Don McKinnon		Minister of Foreign Affairs and</p>
<p>Trade</p>
<p>				    Minister of Pacific Island Affairs</p>
<p>				    Minister for Disarmament &amp; Arms</p>
<p>Controls</p>
<p>    Bill Birch		  Minister of Finance</p>
<p>				    Minister of Revenue</p>
<p>    Jenny Shipley	     Minister of State Services</p>
<p>				    Minister of State Owned Enterprises</p>
<p>				    (Responsible for all SOEs except</p>
<p>Contact Energy Ltd)</p>
<p>				    Minister of Transport</p>
<p>				    Minister of Accident Rehabilitation</p>
<p>and</p>
<p>				    Compensation Insurance</p>
<p>				    Minister responsible for Radio NZ</p>
<p>    Doug Graham		 Minister of Justice</p>
<p>				    Minister of Courts</p>
<p>				    Minister in Charge of Treaty of</p>
<p>				    Waitangi Negotiations</p>
<p>    Tau Henare (NZF)	  Minister of Maori Affairs</p>
<p>				    Minister of Racing</p>
<p>				    Associate Minister of Sport, Fitness</p>
<p>and</p>
<p>				    Leisure</p>
<p>    Paul East		   Attorney-General</p>
<p>				    Minister of Defence</p>
<p>				    Minister of Corrections</p>
<p>				    Minister in Charge of War Pensions</p>
<p>				    Minister in Charge of the Audit Dept</p>
<p>    Lockwood Smith	    Minister of Agriculture</p>
<p>				    Minister of Forestry</p>
<p>				    Minister for International Trade</p>
<p>				    Minister Responsible for Contact</p>
<p>Energy Ltd  </p>
<p>    Peter McCardle (NZF)    Minister of Employment</p>
<p>    Wyatt Creech		Minister of Education</p>
<p>				    Leader of the House</p>
<p>    Simon Upton		 Minister of the Environment</p>
<p>				    Minister of Crown Research</p>
<p>Institutes</p>
<p>				    Minister of Biosecurity</p>
<p>				    Associate Minister of Foreign</p>
<p>Affairs and Trade</p>
<p>    Jack Elder (NZF)	  Minister of Police</p>
<p>				    Minister of Internal Affairs</p>
<p>				    Minister of Civil Defence</p>
<p>    Bill English		Minister of Health</p>
<p>    John Luxton		 Minister of Commerce</p>
<p>				    Minister of Fisheries</p>
<p>				    Minister of Lands</p>
<p>				    Minister of Industry</p>
<p>				    Associate Minister of Agriculture</p>
<p>    Maurice Williamson	Minister of Research, Science and</p>
<p>				    Technology</p>
<p>				    Minister of Communications</p>
<p>				    Minister of Information Technology</p>
<p>				    Minister of Statistics</p>
<p>    John Delamere (NZF)     Associate Treasurer</p>
<p>				    Minister in Charge of the Valuation</p>
<p>Dept</p>
<p>				    Minister in Charge of the Public</p>
<p>Trust Office</p>
<p>    Murray McCully	    Minister of Housing</p>
<p>				    Minister of Tourism</p>
<p>				    Minister of Sport, Fitness and</p>
<p>Leisure</p>
<p>    Max Bradford		Minister of Labour</p>
<p>				    Minister of Immigration</p>
<p>				    Minister of Energy</p>
<p>				    Minister of Business Development</p>
<p>    Roger Sowry		 Minister of Social Welfare</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------  </p>
<p>MINISTERS OUTSIDE CABINET:</p>
<p>    Brian Donnelly	    Minister Responsible for the</p>
<p>Education Review Office</p>
<p>				    Associate Minister of Education</p>
<p>    Christine Fletcher	Minister of Women's Affairs</p>
<p>				    Minister of Cultural Affairs</p>
<p>				    Minister of Local Government</p>
<p>    Nick Smith		  Minister of Conservation</p>
<p>				    Associate Minister of Education</p>
<p>				    Associate Minister of Social Welfare</p>
<p>    Deborah Morris	    Minister of Youth Affairs</p>
<p>				    Associate Minister for Accident</p>
<p>				    Rehabilitation and Compensation</p>
<p>Insurance</p>
<p>				    Associate Minister for the</p>
<p>Environment</p>
<p>    Neil Kirton		 Minister of Customs</p>
<p>				    Associate Minister of Health</p>
<p>    Robyn McDonald	    Minister for Senior Citizens</p>
<p>				    Minister of Consumer Affairs</p>
